conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:30:52-07:00","id":99229,"title":"","content":"As time goes on and the PCs become more a part of the world, I think the game has gotten more and more interesting. I know you have recently had a few PCs become NPCs and a few new PCs join the game. Has this been difficult for you as ST?<br /> <br /> Presumably, the older PCs already have some connections in the city and if I recall correctly even have some of the signatures of Primogen which are required to graduate from the kiddie pool in Hartford.<br /> <br /> Also, it seems the carthians of the kiddie pool have decided to split up the territory for themselves. Can you give us an idea of the current population of the kiddie pool and how many of them are carthians? The reason I am wanting to know is I wonder if they can succeed in setting it up this way.<br /> <br /> Another question: I have noticed that frenzying during feeding is a semi-regular occurrence. Is this because their sires have not taught them well? Is the vitae economy so strict that finding oneself low on blood is common? Do your PCs just have low resolve/composure? etc?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There Are Four Lights!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/92949-baltimore-the-kiddie-pool-saga-pics-maps-and-links\" target=\"_blank\">[Actual Play] Baltimore: The Kiddie Pool Saga</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/64-figurehead","name":"figurehead","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar64_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:57:01-07:00","id":99260,"title":"","content":"In answering these, I'm only writing official information, which can be easily learned by the PCs (for obvious reasons).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10420-play-report-hartford?p=99229#post99229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As time goes on and the PCs become more a part of the world, I think the game has gotten more and more interesting. I know you have recently had a few PCs become NPCs and a few new PCs join the game. Has this been difficult for you as ST?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as hard as it could have been, since the PCs who dropped were easy to split away from the party IC as well (due to them joining a covenant the rest of the party was not interested in). So moving the characters out was quite easy <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Moving the new characters in.. wasn't too hard either, since we built their backstories to accommodate it as much as possible( setting up Amir as a friend and the two new characters as old time colleagues).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10420-play-report-hartford?p=99229#post99229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presumably, the older PCs already have some connections in the city and if I recall correctly even have some of the signatures of Primogen which are required to graduate from the kiddie pool in Hartford.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they don't have any signatures, yet. However, as the scale and importance of events is going up, they should be able to start obtaining them quite soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10420-play-report-hartford?p=99229#post99229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it seems the carthians of the kiddie pool have decided to split up the territory for themselves. Can you give us an idea of the current population of the kiddie pool and how many of them are carthians? The reason I am wanting to know is I wonder if they can succeed in setting it up this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. There are currently X coteries in the kiddie pool (all loners have disappeared. Harry - burned in trial, Aiste - turned citizen, Oliver - joined with Tauras, Katerina).<br /> They are:<br /> Daniel's coterie. Consists of Daniel, a Carthian ventrue, sibling of Tauras. Kendalas Kyfas, a Ordo Dracul Gangrel and Emersonas Bohas, unaligned Gangrel.<br /> Erika's coterie. Consists of Erika, Carthian ventrue, Antonijus May, Carthian Mekhet, Zacharajus, unaligned Nosferatu and Donaldas Bankorfas, unaligned Daeva.<br /> Tina's coterie. Consists of Tina Wats, Ordo Dracul mekhet, Albertas Rydas, Lancea Sanctum nosferatu<br /> Tauras' coterie. Constis of Tauras, Acolyte Ventrue. Katerina, Acolyte Gangrel. Oliver, unaligned nosferatu.<br /> Teodoras' coterie. Consists of Teodoras, Acolyte ventrue and Barbara, acolyte Daeva.<br /> PCs coterie. Consists of all the PCs. To remind you. Markas - member of Ordo Dracul and Carthians nosferatu. Albert - wannabe Invictus, planning to join them, and already creating ties to go in that direction. He's a Ventrue . Rhea - Lancea Sanctum Mekhet. Amir - Unaligned Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Carthians expect to come out at the top, because 3 out of 6 coteries contain one. One (tina's) is considered quite weak. The only real threat to this arrangement is the Circle of the Crone aligned Coteries. But they are likely to cause trouble only if somebody tries to move against their feeding grounds (The Point and The Spa).<br /> <br /> Does this answer the question? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>figurehead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10420-play-report-hartford?p=99229#post99229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question: I have noticed that frenzying during feeding is a semi-regular occurrence. Is this because their sires have not taught them well? Is the vitae economy so strict that finding oneself low on blood is common? Do your PCs just have low resolve/composure? etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the start of the chronicle, I used to overdo the &quot;roll for frenzy when feeding&quot; thing. Nowadays I only ask for it if the vampires have 4 or less vitae. (Albert hunted with 4 or 2.. can't remember right now). So I'd guess it's because I was over strict with the frenzy rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> should be better now.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":294,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","user":"Griautis","date":". 03-26-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T09:59:29-07:00","id":99261,"title":"","content":"Also it's very cool to hear that the game is getting more interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I also feel the same way. The further we go, the better this game gets <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: Sry for double post. First message got too long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T10:39:15-07:00","id":102770,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.evernote.com/shard/s263/sh/85ef25be-c239-4513-b8c4-e0469d5147ee/e23a30a6f3ac1a678cb192ab7b170c21\" target=\"_blank\">Hartford: Twenty Fourth Session - The Invictus Bounty</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reacti